### Create Permanent Alias
#### Open .bashrc (The .bashrc file is a script file that’s executed when a user logs in. The file itself contains a series of configurations for the terminal session.) 
$ [text editor] ~/.bashrc
#### Modify the file so it would include the new alias adding:
alias [command alias]='[command to be aliased]'



